# What must never be committed.
#
# The keys below are generated on first start and are specific to one
# installation. `.secret` signs session cookies; `.data_key` is what makes the
# encrypted columns readable at all. Either one in a public repository is a
# complete compromise of any instance using it, and git remembers: a key
# pushed once stays in the history after it is deleted.

.secret
.data_key
.vapid_keys
.ref_keys
.smtp_config
.stripe_key
.qtsp_config
.eid_config
.ai_config
seam.env

# The database and everything uploaded into it. Contains demo companies, test
# accounts and whatever has been tried out locally.
seam.db
seam.db-wal
seam.db-shm
uploads/
backups/

# Local Python.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# Test leftovers.
tests/_restored.db
tests/load_check.json

# Editors and operating systems.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
